ui.wiring.help.need_dac=Add a DAC, edit its Verilog, then run Analyze/Build.
ui.wiring.help.route_open=The powered audio path is incomplete.
ui.wiring.help.problem_rtl_not_built=The DAC RTL has not been analyzed and built.
ui.wiring.help.problem_dac_bus=The discrete DAC output bus is not wired.
ui.wiring.help.problem_supply_short=The DC supply +V and return nets are shorted.
ui.wiring.help.problem_line_level=The current amplifier is line-level and cannot drive a speaker.
ui.wiring.help.problem_unpowered_stage=The complementary Class-AB output stage is not correctly powered or driven.
ui.wiring.help.need_rtl_build=Open the DAC editor and run Analyze/Build with Verilator.
ui.wiring.help.need_remove_short=Separate the supply +V and return nets before starting simulation.
ui.wiring.help.need_output_pair=Add complementary NPN and PNP output transistors after the powered driver.
ui.wiring.help.need_bus_fmt=Check the DAC buses (L %d/16, R %d/16), powered driver, output pair, and speaker connection.
ui.wiring.help.return_open=A speaker negative/return path is open, so that channel is muted.
ui.wiring.help.need_return=Wire LEFT_NEG and RIGHT_NEG to Analog Ground.
ui.wiring.help.speaker_risk=The route works, but the output stage can damage the speaker.
ui.wiring.help.need_dc_block=Add a 1000uF or larger series DC-blocking capacitor per channel.
ui.wiring.help.need_ballast=Add 0.1-0.47 ohm emitter ballast resistors to the NPN/PNP output pair.
ui.wiring.help.one_channel=Only one channel reaches the speaker.
ui.wiring.help.need_stereo_symmetry=Mirror the working channel's DAC, filter, volume, amplifier, and return wiring.
ui.wiring.help.incomplete_bus_fmt=The DAC route works, but its discrete buses are incomplete (L %d/16, R %d/16).
ui.wiring.help.need_all_bits=Connect every DAC output bit through the intended resistor network.
ui.wiring.help.dac_weight_fault=All DAC bits are connected, but the resistor ratios produce incorrect bit weights.
ui.wiring.help.need_dac_ratios=Compare every DAC branch resistance and tolerance with the intended ladder value.
ui.wiring.help.amp_underpowered=The amplifier cannot deliver even half of the speaker's rated power.
ui.wiring.help.need_amp_supply=Increase supply voltage/current capacity or lower the amplifier gain and speaker power target.
ui.wiring.help.amp_bias_fault=The Class-AB output bias is incorrect or lacks thermal tracking.
ui.wiring.help.need_bias_fix=Use two suitable bias drops and thermally couple them to the output transistor heatsink.
ui.wiring.help.amp_bandwidth_fault=A driver has less than 20 kHz closed-loop bandwidth.
ui.wiring.help.need_driver_bandwidth=Raise gain-bandwidth or reduce closed-loop gain, then check the response graph.
ui.wiring.help.stereo_mismatch=Left and right frequency responses differ by more than 1 dB.
ui.wiring.help.need_filter_match=Match both channels' resistor, capacitor, inductor, and potentiometer values.
ui.wiring.help.high_distortion=The route works, but modeled distortion exceeds 5%.
ui.wiring.help.need_distortion_check=Inspect DAC accuracy, bias, slew rate, output loading, and the live FFT.
ui.wiring.help.circuit_ok=The powered stereo route and speaker protection are complete.
ui.wiring.help.tutorial=Quick build order
ui.wiring.help.step1=1. PC Digital Audio -> DAC I2S inputs.
ui.wiring.help.step2=2. DAC output bits -> resistor ladder -> reconstruction LPF/buffer.
ui.wiring.help.step3=3. Buffer -> 10k-100k volume potentiometer -> voltage driver.
ui.wiring.help.step4=4. Powered driver -> bias network -> complementary NPN/PNP output stage.
ui.wiring.help.step5=5. Emitter resistors -> large DC-blocking capacitor -> speaker.
ui.wiring.help.step6=6. Connect all returns, build RTL, then start simulation and inspect Signal Analyzer.
